<title>USA: First Commonwealth to buy Mo. dental plan.</title>
<headline>First Commonwealth to buy Mo. dental plan.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Commonwealth Inc, a managed dental benefits company, said Thursday it entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Champion Dental Services Inc, a St. Louis-based prepaid dental plan.</p>
<p>It will acquire Champion Dental for $5.3 million from Group Health Plan Inc, a St. Louis medical health maintenance organization that is a wholly owned subidiary of Coventry Corp.</p>
<p>Champion provides preventive and comprehensive managed dental care benefits to about 60,000 enrollees.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
